down.\n    *   The proposal promises to turn compliance into a \"fixed platform cost,\" which liberates researchers to focus on the intellectual merit of their work rather than regulatory bookkeeping.\n    *   It ensures consistency across projects, which is better for longitudinal studies or meta-analyses of model performance/failures (scientific impact).\n\n    *   Rationale: By automating regulatory record-keeping at the infrastructure level, this proposal removes significant operational friction and \"compliance tax\" from individual research projects, enabling faster iteration on the knowledge frontier. It also ensures a standardized data format for system events, which enhances the reproducibility and auditability of our scientific outputs.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 90 (High value because it protects researcher time/velocity without requiring researchers to become compliance experts).",
