ing anyway (per law), automating the export into a dossier is a sensible technical extension that provides clear output specifications for the dev team.\n    *   It doesn't fundamentally change the technical architecture; it just adds a \"reporting\" requirement.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal effectively turns mandatory logging requirements into a defined set of deliverables, which clarifies engineering specs and leverages existing compliance work to provide tangible value to clients.\n    *   Decision: Approve. (Because it aligns technical output with client needs without introducing prohibitive technical complexity).\n    *   Promise: High, but not 100 because the core effort is Legal/Product; Engineering just provides the data. Let's say 85.\n\n    *   Wait, as a *Development Engineer*, my primary concern is \"technical viability\" and \"speed/quality of prototyping.\"\n    *   Does this proposal slow down prototyping? Not necessarily, provided the reports are generated from existing logs.\n    *   Is it technically viable? Absolutely; exporting data to a template is standard.\n    *   Does it add value? It provides a target for what the \"logs\" should actually look like, which reduces rework.",
