ycles by introducing rigid checkboxes before technical solutions are even viable.\n    *   *Core Conflict:* The EU AI Act requires that high-risk AI systems *technically allow* for recording. P2742 is about a service to certify it. If the system isn't technically capable yet, the certification service is useless. As a Dev Engineer, my concern is building the capability, not selling the certificate. This proposal diverts engineering resources (staffing two engineers) toward auditing and marketing rather than developing the actual logging infrastructure required by law.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal describes a business model for compliance certification rather than a technical implementation of the required logging capabilities; it diverts engineering resources away from development and prototyping toward administrative auditing.\n    *   Decision: reject.\n    *   Promise: 15 (It's not technically useless if we already have the logs, but as an R&D engineer focusing on viability/prototyping, this is a distraction).",
