es recording events for traceability. If DP/federated aggregation obscures the data *too much*, it might fail the legal requirement (especially Annex III point 1(a) which asks for \"input data\"). However, the proposal is to *research* how to do this while satisfying the duties. The research itself has high value even if the result shows some constraints.\n    *   Does it align with my domain? Yes. It's about a \"Research Track,\" \"prototyping,\" and \"publishing.\"\n\n    *   *Rationale:* This proposal transforms a mundane regulatory burden into an opportunity for high-impact research on the intersection of privacy-preserving technologies and AI auditability, potentially advancing the state-of-the-art in compliant logging.\n    *   *Decision:* approve.\n    *   *Promise:* 85 (High because it leverages PhD talent to create a publishable/licensable asset from a mandatory requirement).",
