formance over time.\n    *   *Compliance Link:* Recital 71 emphasizes keeping records \"up to date... throughout the lifetime.\" If schemas drift without versioning, the record is effectively lost or corrupted, undermining the ability to verify compliance scientifically.\n\n    *   The proposal is highly practical and essential for any large-scale R&D effort that intends to maintain scientific rigor over long lifecycles. It prevents \"data rot\" in the logging system.\n    *   It allows researchers to perform retrospective analysis on old versions using new tools (or vice versa), which is critical for understanding the evolution of AI capabilities and risks.\n\n    *   Rationale: Consistent, versioned logs are essential for the longitudinal analysis of AI behavior and ensure that empirical evidence remains accessible as systems evolve. This infrastructure transforms a regulatory burden into a scientific asset by preserving the interpretability of historical performance data.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 90 (Very high because it's foundational for research integrity in an evolving system).",
